# Quote: Mario Bunge - Treatise on Basic Philosophy - Epistemology & Methodology III - Part II

> Freud has been said to have taken obscenity out of sex, which was a triumph for the newer, more liberal morality. But it is also true that, by greatly exaggerating the role of sexuality in mental life, by framing fantastic conjectures about both, and by not even attempting to test those conjectures, he made no serious contribution to the study of either sexuality or mind: he just opened a can of worms.

